<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-MMI buys FAI insurance units.</title>
<headline>RTRS-MMI buys FAI insurance units.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Insurer MMI Ltd said on Monday it has agreed to buy the general insurance operations of FAI Insurances Ltd in New Zealand, Fiji and Papua New Guinea.  </p>
<p>MMI said conditional contracts had been exchanged, and completion of the sale was conditional on regulatory approval and due diligence. No price was disclosed.</p>
<p>The sale was expected to be completed by early August 1997.</p>
<p>MMI, 38 percent owned by Germany's Allianz AG, has been expanding its Asian operations in a link-up with the German insurance giant.</p>
<p>MMI said in May the two groups had signed a memorandum of understanding with an Indian company to consider entering the Indian health insurance market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
